    "text": "Reading and Writing: Question 25In her poetry collection Thomas and Beulah, Rita Dove interweaves the titular characters’ personal stories with broader historical narratives. She places Thomas’s journey from the American South to the Midwest in the early 1900s within the larger context of the Great Migration. ______blank Dove sets events from Beulah’s personal life against the backdrop of the US Civil Rights Movement.Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?Specifically,Thus,Regardless,Similarly,",
