    "section": "SAT Practice 4 - May 22, 2026",
    "text": "Reading and Writing: Question 26When designing costumes for film, American artist Suttirat Larlarb typically custom fits the garments to each actor. ______blank for the film Sunshine, in which astronauts must reignite a dying Sun, she designed a golden spacesuit and had a factory reproduce it in a few standard sizes; lacking a tailor-made quality, the final creations reflected the ungainliness of actual spacesuits.Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?Nevertheless,Thus,Likewise,Moreover,",
    "html": "<h3 class=\"cb-margin-bottom-16\">Reading and Writing: Question 26</h3><div class=\"cb-margin-bottom-16\"><p>When designing costumes for film, American artist Suttirat Larlarb typically custom fits the garments to each actor. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> for the film <em>Sunshine</em>, in which astronauts must reignite a dying Sun, she designed a golden spacesuit and had a factory reproduce it in a few standard sizes; lacking a tailor-made quality, the final creations reflected the ungainliness of actual spacesuits.</p></div><div><p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p></div><ol type=\"A\" class=\"answer-options cb-margin-top-16\"><li class=\"\"><div class=\"\"><p>Nevertheless,</p></div></li><li class=\"\"><div class=\"\"><p>Thus,</p></div></li><li class=\"\"><div class=\"\"><p>Likewise,</p></div></li><li class=\"\"><div class=\"\"><p>Moreover,</p></div></li></ol>"
